Node.js LTS and pnpm

Install:
  Install missing pnpm, pnpx and Node.js LTS; configure PATH and create fallback npm/npx links when those commands are unavailable.

Upgrade:
  Update pnpm and Node.js LTS installed under PNPM_HOME; repair pnpx and command links.

Status:
  Report Node.js and pnpm command locations and versions.
  Report pnpx, npm and npx command locations.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  PNPM_HOME: ~/.local/share/pnpm by default
  A custom PNPM_HOME must be an absolute path without colons or line breaks; it is saved for later operations.
  Existing Node.js and pnpm commands can satisfy installation; upgrade only updates versions managed under PNPM_HOME.
  Shell configuration adds PNPM_HOME/bin, PNPM_HOME and ~/.local/bin to PATH.
  Fallback npm/npx links invoke pnpm/pnpx; existing commands are preserved, and fallback links yield to commands available elsewhere on PATH.
  Open a new terminal after installation to load the environment.
